<graph edgedefault="undirected"><node id="Bank">
  <data key="d0">Bank</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Bank is a financial institution that primarily accepts deposits from the public and provides a variety of banking services. These services include managing deposit accounts, offering loans, and providing interest payments on deposits. The Bank is responsible for ensuring the security and management of customer deposits, as well as offering additional banking products such as debit cards and mobile banking.

In addition to standard account management, the Bank has policies in place regarding different types of accounts and services tailored for customers with special needs. It also plays a critical role in handling claims related to deceased customers, which includes managing legal documents and processing claims and payments associated with their deposit accounts. Furthermore, the Bank is responsible for safe deposit lockers, enabling customers to securely store valuables.

The Bank engages in various customer service initiatives, including awareness campaigns and handling customer complaints, thereby emphasizing its commitment to client satisfaction and transparency in all banking transactions. Overall, the Bank serves as a comprehensive financial institution dedicated to facilitating a wide range of banking needs for its customers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741497</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deposit">
  <data key="d0">Deposit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Funds that are accepted by the bank from depositors, forming a key element of the banking system.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Depositors">
  <data key="d0">Depositors</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Individuals or entities that place their funds into deposit accounts in banks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Banking Regulation Act, 1949">
  <data key="d0">Banking Regulation Act, 1949</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Legislation that enshrines the regulatory framework for banking and the rights of depositors in India.&lt;SEP&gt;An act that provides a framework for banking regulation in India, including provisions for locker operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reserve Bank of India">
  <data key="d0">Reserve Bank of India</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The central bank of India, responsible for regulating the issue and supply of the Indian rupee and overseeing the banking industry.&lt;SEP&gt;The central banking institution of India, responsible for regulating the issuance and supply of the Indian rupee and overseeing the monetary policy of the country.&lt;SEP&gt;The central banking institution of India, responsible for regulating the issue and supply of the Indian rupee and overseeing the Indian banking system.&lt;SEP&gt;The central banking institution in India, responsible for regulating the country's monetary policy and overseeing financial institutions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740931</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unity Small Finance Bank Limited">
  <data key="d0">Unity Small Finance Bank Limited</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific bank that offers various deposit products and governs the conduct of deposit accounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Interest Rates">
  <data key="d0">Interest Rates</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The cost of borrowing or the earnings on deposits, regulated by the Reserve Bank of India.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Financial System">
  <data key="d0">Financial System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The system that includes banks and other financial institutions that provide services related to money management.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deposit Accounts">
  <data key="d0">Deposit Accounts</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Accounts that hold deposited funds and are subject to terms and conditions as outlined by the bank.&lt;SEP&gt;Financial accounts where individuals deposit money, which may involve claims in the event of the account holder's death.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Demand Deposits">
  <data key="d0">Demand Deposits</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A category of deposit products that are withdrawable on demand, including various types of accounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time Deposits">
  <data key="d0">Time Deposits</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A category of deposit products where the money is deposited for a fixed period, including recurring and fixed deposits.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Savings Account">
  <data key="d0">Savings Account</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of demand deposit that has restrictions on the number and amount of withdrawals.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of bank account offered by the Bank that allows individuals to deposit money and earn interest on savings.&lt;SEP&gt;A deposit account held at a bank that pays interest but has limited transactions.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of bank account that allows individuals to save money while earning interest, which can be involved in claims settlements upon the account holder's death.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of bank account that allows individuals to deposit money and earn interest on their savings.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-mm-table-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-mm-table-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basic Savings Bank Deposit Account">
  <data key="d0">Basic Savings Bank Deposit Account</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific type of savings account offered by the Bank under guidelines set by the RBI.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Current Account">
  <data key="d0">Current Account</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of demand deposit that allows unrestricted withdrawals up to the account balance or an agreed amount.&lt;SEP&gt;A bank account that allows for frequent transactions and is available to individuals and businesses, provided by the Bank.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of bank account that allows for numerous deposits and withdrawals and typically does not earn interest.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of bank account that provides easy access to funds and allows for frequent transactions, relevant in the context of claims settlement for deceased account holders.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-mm-table-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cash Credit">
  <data key="d0">Cash Credit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A credit facility offered by the Bank that allows for borrowing against a deposit account.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Overdraft">
  <data key="d0">Overdraft</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A facility allowing an account holder to withdraw more money than is available in the account.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RBI">
  <data key="d0">RBI</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Reserve Bank of India, which sets guidelines and policies for banking operations in India.&lt;SEP&gt;The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) is the central banking institution of India, which regulates the issuance and supply of the Indian rupee and oversees banking operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="KYC">
  <data key="d0">KYC</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Know Your Customer, a set of guidelines for verifying the identity of customers in banking.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PAN">
  <data key="d0">PAN</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
