  <data key="d0">Mobile Banking</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A service provided by the Bank allowing customers to perform banking transactions via mobile devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="WhatsApp Banking">
  <data key="d0">WhatsApp Banking</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A service provided by the Bank that allows customers to access banking services through the WhatsApp platform.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Internet Banking">
  <data key="d0">Internet Banking</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A service provided by the Bank to permit customers to conduct financial transactions through the internet.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ATM Network">
  <data key="d0">ATM Network</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">A system that includes the Bank's own ATMs as well as those of other banks, allowing customers to access cash and banking services.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NEFT">
  <data key="d0">NEFT</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">National Electronic Funds Transfer, an electronic payment method offered by the Bank for transferring funds between accounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RTGS">
  <data key="d0">RTGS</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Real Time Gross Settlement, a system used by the Bank for the immediate transfer of funds between accounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Statement of Account">
  <data key="d0">Statement of Account</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A monthly report provided by the Bank to account holders detailing account activity and balances.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joint Account">
  <data key="d0">Joint Account</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An account held by more than one individual, allowing all named account holders to access and manage funds collectively.&lt;SEP&gt;A bank account shared between two or more individuals, where claims procedures can be influenced by multiple depositors' arrangements upon the death of a holder.&lt;SEP&gt;An account held by two or more individuals, where the terms of the account dictate how funds are accessed upon the death of an account holder.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-mm-table-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-mm-table-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Account Operations">
  <data key="d0">Account Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A section outlining the procedures and rules regarding the opening and management of various types of accounts, including individual, minor, and joint accounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Minor Account">
  <data key="d0">Minor Account</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of savings account that can be opened for a minor by a legally appointed guardian, which can be operated by the guardian or, under certain conditions, by the minor themselves.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Power of Attorney">
  <data key="d0">Power of Attorney</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A legal authorization allowing someone else to operate an account on behalf of the account holder, which must be registered with the Bank.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mandate">
  <data key="d0">Mandate</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An authorization given by the account holder(s) to another person to operate the account, applicable particularly for NRI customers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nomination">
  <data key="d0">Nomination</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A facility that allows account holders to designate a nominee for their account, which can be changed or cancelled at any time.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Depositor">
  <data key="d0">Depositor</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A depositor is an individual who places money into an account at the Bank, and may nominate a person to receive funds in case of the depositor's death.&lt;SEP&gt;The individual who holds a term deposit with the bank and is responsible for its management until death.&lt;SEP&gt;An individual who holds an account at a bank and is the owner of deposited funds.&lt;SEP&gt;An individual or entity that holds an account and has certain rights associated with deposits in the account.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-mm-table-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nominee">
  <data key="d0">Nominee</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The nominee is a person to whom the Bank will pay the deposit amount upon the death of the account holder if the beneficiary is a minor.&lt;SEP&gt;An individual designated by the depositor to receive the benefits of the term deposit upon the depositor's death.&lt;SEP&gt;An individual appointed by a depositor to receive the funds from the depositor's account in the event of their death.&lt;SEP&gt;An individual designated to receive the assets of a deceased depositor from the bank.&lt;SEP&gt;An individual designated to receive the benefits from a deceased's account upon their death.&lt;SEP&gt;An individual designated by the locker hirer to receive the contents of the locker in the event of the hirer's death.&lt;SEP&gt;An individual designated to receive the benefits from an account or locker upon the account holder's death.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Senior Citizen">
  <data key="d0">Senior Citizen</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A resident Indian aged over 60 years, eligible for higher interest rates on fixed deposits as stipulated by the Bank.&lt;SEP&gt;An individual who is classified as elderly and has the same savings limits as differently abled customers in banking services.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740931</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Illiterate Person">
  <data key="d0">Illiterate Person</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">An individual who may open a deposit account at the Bank under certain conditions, even if they cannot read or write.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Visually Challenged Person">
  <data key="d0">Visually Challenged Person</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">An individual with visual impairments who can open and operate their account with assistance from Bank officials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transgender Person">
  <data key="d0">Transgender Person</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">An individual who identifies as transgender and is recognized as 'Third Gender' by the Bank when opening an account or conducting transactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guardian">
  <data key="d0">Guardian</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A legal guardian appointed to care for a disabled person or minor, responsible for managing their financial accounts as specified by various laws.&lt;SEP&gt;A responsible adult appointed to act on behalf of a minor nominee to claim locker contents.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Local Level Committees">
  <data key="d0">Local Level Committees</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Committees established under the National Trust for the Welfare of Persons with Autism, Cerebral Palsy, Mental Retardation and Multiple Disabilities Act, 1999, responsible for supporting the financial needs of disabled individuals.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="District Courts">
  <data key="d0">District Courts</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Legal institutions that appoint guardians for individuals under the Mental Health Act, 1987, enabling the establishment of financial accounts for those individuals.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Regulator">
  <data key="d0">Regulator</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Government or statutory authorities that issue guidelines for opening accounts for non-resident individuals in accordance with applicable laws.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="National Trust for the Welfare of Persons with Autism, Cerebral Palsy, Mental Retardation and Multiple Disabilities Act, 1999">
  <data key="d0">National Trust for the Welfare of Persons with Autism, Cerebral Palsy, Mental Retardation and Multiple Disabilities Act, 1999</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An act that provides for the welfare of persons with disabilities and allows banking facilities for individuals covered under it.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="The Mental Health Act, 1987">
  <data key="d0">The Mental Health Act, 1987</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An act that establishes legal provisions for the care and treatment of individuals with mental health issues, including provisions for opening bank accounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Term Deposit">
  <data key="d0">Term Deposit</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A deposit that is made for a fixed term and typically earns a higher interest rate than a savings account.&lt;SEP&gt;A financial product offered by the bank where a fixed sum of money is deposited for a specified period, during which interest is earned.&lt;SEP&gt;A financial product that locks in funds for a specific period in exchange for a higher interest rate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-mm-table-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Domestic Non-Resident Ordinary Account">
  <data key="d0">Domestic Non-Resident Ordinary Account</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of bank account designed for non-resident Indians to manage their income and savings in India.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non-Resident External Account">
  <data key="d0">Non-Resident External Account</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of bank account in India that allows non-resident Indians to manage their income earned abroad in Indian rupees.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bulk Deposits">
  <data key="d0">Bulk Deposits</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Large sums of money deposited at the bank, often attracting different interest rates than regular deposits.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deposit Interest Rate Card">
  <data key="d0">Deposit Interest Rate Card</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A document or system maintained by the bank that outlines the interest rates applicable to various deposit accounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Interest Rate Framework">
  <data key="d0">Interest Rate Framework</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The structured set of rules and guidelines governing how interest rates are determined and applied by a bank.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Interest Rate">
  <data key="d0">Interest Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The percentage of the deposit amount that the bank pays as interest for the duration the term deposit remains with the bank.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NRE Deposit">
  <data key="d0">NRE Deposit</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Non-Resident External deposit scheme that allows non-residents to hold accounts in Indian banks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NRO Deposit">
  <data key="d0">NRO Deposit</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Non-Resident Ordinary deposit scheme that allows non-residents to manage their income earned in India.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Master Policy on Customer Service">
  <data key="d0">Master Policy on Customer Service</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The overarching guidance document that includes various policies related to customer service and term deposit management.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tax Deduction at Source (TDS)">
  <data key="d0">Tax Deduction at Source (TDS)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A tax obligation where the bank is required to deduct a certain percentage of tax from the interest paid on term deposits.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Legal Heirs">
  <data key="d0">Legal Heirs</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Individuals entitled to the assets or rights of the deceased depositor, who may request the termination of the term deposit.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals who are entitled to inherit the property or assets of a deceased person.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals entitled to inherit the assets of a deceased person, significant in the claims settlement process for accounts with nominations.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals entitled to inherit the rights to the outstanding amounts in the account after the death of the account holders.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals who are entitled to inherit the property or assets of a deceased individual, particularly in the context of bank accounts.&lt;SEP&gt;Persons entitled to access the locker in the event of A or B's death, as specified in the operational instructions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-mm-table-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-mm-table-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-mm-table-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-mm-table-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Penalty for Premature Withdrawal">
  <data key="d0">Penalty for Premature Withdrawal</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A fee charged by the bank for early withdrawal of a term deposit before the agreed-upon maturity period.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NRE Deposits">
  <data key="d0">NRE Deposits</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">NRE (Non-Resident External) deposits are bank accounts for non-resident Indians to manage their income earned outside India, allowing them to hold foreign currency and maintain domestic savings.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NRO Deposits">
  <data key="d0">NRO Deposits</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">NRO (Non-Resident Ordinary) deposits allow non-resident Indians to manage income earned in India, which can be maintained in Indian rupees and used for local expenses.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scheduled Commercial Banks">
  <data key="d0">Scheduled Commercial Banks</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Scheduled Commercial Banks are banks that are included in the Second Schedule of the Reserve Bank of India Act, providing various banking services to customers, including deposits and loans.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Board of Directors">
  <data key="d0">Board of Directors</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Board of Directors is a group of individuals elected to represent shareholders and oversee the activities of an organization, such as a bank, in accordance with governance standards.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DICGC">
  <data key="d0">DICGC</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Deposit Insurance and Credit Guarantee Corporation of India (DICGC) is an organization that provides deposit insurance to enhance the safety of deposits made by customers with banks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Customer Service Master Policy">
  <data key="d0">Customer Service Master Policy</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Customer Service Master Policy outlines the guidelines and procedures for customer interactions, including deposit handling, account management, and service standards by the bank.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deceased Depositor">
  <data key="d0">Deceased Depositor</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A deceased depositor refers to an individual who held a term deposit account and has passed away, leading to specific policies for the disbursement of funds to designated claimants.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Minor">
  <data key="d0">Minor</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A minor is a person under the age of majority who may have a bank deposit. Specific policies apply to loans or overdrafts taken against their term deposits.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joint Account Holders">
  <data key="d0">Joint Account Holders</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Joint account holders are individuals who share ownership of a bank account and may request changes such as the addition or deletion of names on the account.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inactive Account">
  <data key="d0">Inactive Account</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">An inactive account is one that has not been operated by the customer for a period of one year, prompting banks to notify the account holder of the status change.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dormant Account">
  <data key="d0">Dormant Account</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">A dormant account is an account that has not been operated for two years, requiring the bank to classify it as dormant to ensure the depositor's interest.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unclaimed Deposits">
  <data key="d0">Unclaimed Deposits</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Unclaimed deposits refer to accounts that have not been active for ten years and are transferred to the Reserve Bank of India under specific regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Deposits that have not been claimed or accessed by the depositor or their nominee/legal heir for a specified duration, thus requiring procedures for claiming.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Claimants">
  <data key="d0">Claimants</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Claimants are individuals authorized to make a claim on the funds of a deceased depositor's account, requiring proof of death and identification.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals who submit claims related to deposit accounts or safe deposit lockers, particularly after the account holder's death.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-005</data>
