</node>
<node id="tb-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-0001">
  <data key="d0">tb-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-0001</data>
  <data key="d1">table</data>
  <data key="d2">[Table Name]service_type_savings_limits

The table outlines the savings limits for different types of banking services, specifically Cash Pickup and Cash Delivery, across various customer segments. There are four columns in the table: 'Type of service', 'Savings (individuals)', 'Senior Citizen / Differently Abled', and 'Current Account Customers'. Each row details the maximum allowable savings per instance based on the type of service provided. For Cash Pickup, both individuals and senior citizens or differently abled customers can save up to 20,000, while current account customers have a significantly higher limit of 5 lacs per instance. The same savings limits apply to Cash Delivery, with the same values noted for each customer segment. This suggests uniformity in service limits for individual and senior citizen/differently abled customers, while current account customers have a larger cap. The footnote indicates that these savings limits may change in response to bank policies, adding a layer of variability to the content presented. Overall, the table serves to clarify the maximum savings allowed for different customer categories when utilizing specific banking services, which is essential for customer awareness and financial planning.

[Table Footnotes]# Subject to change from time to time as per banks policy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787740931</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rules of Nomination and Settlement of Claims in Respect of Deceased Customers and Missing Persons">
  <data key="d0">Rules of Nomination and Settlement of Claims in Respect of Deceased Customers and Missing Persons</data>
  <data key="d1">document</data>
  <data key="d2">A set of guidelines relating to the processes of nominating and settling claims for deceased customers and missing persons.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nomination Facility">
  <data key="d0">Nomination Facility</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A tool designed to simplify the settlement of claims for deceased depositors by allowing banks to discharge payment to the nominee upon the depositor's death.&lt;SEP&gt;A service offered by the bank that allows customers to appoint a nominee for their deposit accounts, ensuring a smoother transfer of funds upon the account holder's death.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Survivorship Mandate">
  <data key="d0">Survivorship Mandate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A clause in joint accounts that allows surviving account holders to access the account balance without restriction after the death of one of the co-account holders.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Claim Form">
  <data key="d0">Claim Form</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A form that must be filled and signed by the nominee or claimant to initiate the process of settling claims belonging to a deceased depositor.&lt;SEP&gt;A document (Annex I-B) required to be filled in and signed by the claimant(s) other than those who have signed the letter of disclaimer or no objection for processing claims.&lt;SEP&gt;A document that must be duly filled and signed by the nominee or legal heir to claim the contents of a locker.&lt;SEP&gt;A designated form that must be completed to initiate the claims process with the relevant authorities or organizations.&lt;SEP&gt;A document required for filing a claim related to the accounts of deceased depositors.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-mm-table-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Death Certificate">
  <data key="d0">Death Certificate</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">An official document that verifies the death of an individual, required for processing claims of deceased depositors.&lt;SEP&gt;A document certifying the death of the deceased depositor(s) required for claims processing.&lt;SEP&gt;A vital record that certifies the death of the locker hirer, required for claims.&lt;SEP&gt;An official document issued by a government or authority confirming the date and cause of a person's death.&lt;SEP&gt;A document that officially confirms the death of the account holder, required for claim processing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-mm-table-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Claimant">
  <data key="d0">Claimant</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">An individual who asserts a legal right to receive the assets or benefits from the estate of a deceased depositor, particularly in cases where there is no nominee.&lt;SEP&gt;An individual or entity that submits a claim to the bank regarding the contents of safe deposit lockers or articles in safe custody.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Competent Court">
  <data key="d0">Competent Court</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">An authorized judicial body that can issue orders regarding the distribution of a deceased's assets and can restrain the bank from making payments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Threshold Limit">
  <data key="d0">Threshold Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A specified amount, set at 15 lakh, which determines the processes for settling claims of deceased depositors, specifically differentiating between claims below and above this value.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Officially Valid Document">
  <data key="d0">Officially Valid Document</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A document used to verify the identity and address of the claimant(s) during the claims settlement process.&lt;SEP&gt;A document that verifies the identity and address of the nominee or claimant.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bond of Indemnity">
  <data key="d0">Bond of Indemnity</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A formal agreement required to indemnify the bank against losses related to the claims on safe deposit locker contents.&lt;SEP&gt;A document (Annex I-C) that must be signed by the claimant(s) as part of the claims application.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Letter of Disclaimer">
  <data key="d0">Letter of Disclaimer</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A document (Annex I-D) from non-claimant legal heir(s) confirming that they have no objection to the claims made by others.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Affidavit">
  <data key="d0">Affidavit</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A legal document (Annex I-E) sworn before a Notary Public or Judicial Magistrate regarding the legal heir(s) of the deceased depositor.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Probate of Will">
  <data key="d0">Probate of Will</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A legal document that certifies the validity of a will, which may be used to settle claims without the need for a Bond of Indemnity.&lt;SEP&gt;A legal document confirming the validity of a deceased person's will, used for settling claims regarding the estate.&lt;SEP&gt;A legal process whereby a will is validated by the court before the estate can be distributed.&lt;SEP&gt;Probate of Will is a legal process through which a deceased person's will is validated and their estate is administered.&lt;SEP&gt;A legal process that validates a will and grants authority to executors to manage the estate of the deceased.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Letter of Administration">
  <data key="d0">Letter of Administration</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">A legal document issued by a court, allowing a person to manage the estate of a deceased individual, facilitating claim settlements.&lt;SEP&gt;A court document that authorizes an individual to administer the estate of a deceased person, relevant in claims settlement.&lt;SEP&gt;A document issued by a court to appoint an administrator for the estate of a deceased person when there is no will.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Court Order">
  <data key="d0">Court Order</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A directive issued by a court that can affect the settlement of claims involving deceased customers or missing persons.&lt;SEP&gt;A directive issued by a court of law that requires someone to act in accordance with the law or specific judicial decision.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sequencing Certificate">
  <data key="d0">Sequencing Certificate</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">A legal document that certifies the sequence of events regarding the deceased to resolve claims.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Missing Person">
  <data key="d0">Missing Person</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">An individual whose whereabouts are unknown and necessitates specific claims procedures for their account.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FIR">
  <data key="d0">FIR</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A First Information Report, a document required for claiming settlements regarding missing persons.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non-traceable Report">
  <data key="d0">Non-traceable Report</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A report issued by police authorities, serving as a replacement for a death certificate in missing person claims.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Survivor">
  <data key="d0">Survivor</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">An individual who retains rights to the locker and its contents following the death of one of the joint locker hirers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Locker Hirer">
  <data key="d0">Locker Hirer</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">An individual who has hired a safe deposit locker to store valuables.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Minor Nominee">
  <data key="d0">Minor Nominee</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A minor individual designated as a nominee for the locker contents, requiring a guardian to act on their behalf.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deceased Customer">
  <data key="d0">Deceased Customer</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A customer who has passed away and who had previously hired a safe deposit locker.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Will">
  <data key="d0">Will</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A legal document left by a deceased locker hirer that specifies the distribution of their assets.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Successor Certificate">
  <data key="d0">Successor Certificate</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A legal document that establishes the rightful heirs to a deceased person's estate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Legal Heir Certificate">
  <data key="d0">Legal Heir Certificate</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A document issued by a competent authority confirming the legal heirs of the deceased.&lt;SEP&gt;A legal document that establishes a person as the legal heir to the deceased, typically issued by a competent authority.&lt;SEP&gt;A document that establishes the legal heirs of the deceased, necessary for processing claims.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-mm-table-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Annex I-A">
  <data key="d0">Annex I-A</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A specified form related to the claim process for contents of the locker.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex I-A is an annexure providing specific documentation requirements related to claims for accounts with nominee or survivorship clauses.&lt;SEP&gt;An appendix containing additional information or forms relevant to claims with nominees or survivorships.&lt;SEP&gt;Referenced additional documentation required for the settlement claims process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-mm-table-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Annex I-B">
  <data key="d0">Annex I-B</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A specified form required for claim submission by legal heirs.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex I-B is an annexure that outlines the claim form necessary for claims in various scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;An appendix providing supplementary details or forms related to simplified claims procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;Referenced additional documentation required for the settlement claims process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-mm-table-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Annex I-D">
  <data key="d0">Annex I-D</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A specified form for a letter of disclaimer from non-claimant legal heirs.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex I-D is an annexure that provides guidelines for disclaimer or no objection letters.&lt;SEP&gt;An appendix containing no objection letters or disclaimers needed during the claims process.&lt;SEP&gt;Referenced additional documentation required for the settlement claims process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-mm-table-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Annex I-E">
  <data key="d0">Annex I-E</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">An affidavit regarding the legal heirs sworn before a notary public or judge.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex I-E is an annexure that specifies the need for a legal heir certificate or declaration by a third party.&lt;SEP&gt;An appendix that contains legal heir certificates or declarations required for claims in the absence of nominees.&lt;SEP&gt;Referenced additional documentation required for the settlement claims process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-mm-table-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Annex I-F">
  <data key="d0">Annex I-F</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">An inventory form used during the handover of locker contents.&lt;SEP&gt;An appendix including the inventory form required in various claims situations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Annex I-G">
  <data key="d0">Annex I-G</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">An inventory form used for the return of articles in safe custody.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
