<node id="tb-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-0002">
  <data key="d0">tb-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-0002</data>
  <data key="d1">table</data>
  <data key="d2">[Table Name]settlement_of_claims_with_nomination

This table outlines the processes and outcomes associated with various types of accounts with nomination in the context of claims settlement. It consists of 8 rows and 11 columns, detailing different scenarios based on the account nature and depositor arrangements, specifically focusing on Savings and Current Accounts, Term Deposit Accounts, and procedures for premature withdrawal. The columns are structured to show the nature of the account, the status of the depositor (single or joint), and the legal heirs or nominees involved upon death. The first column enumerates the types of accounts, while the subsequent columns differentiate the claims process based on how the accounts are operated (single depositor, joint accounts with various agreements). Merged cells indicate grouped information, for example, the joint account categories are combined under 2 or more columns. Notably, for Joint A/c operated jointly, claims can be made by legal heirs or surviving depositors in multiple scenarios, while nominations are highlighted in situations of maturity and premature withdrawal claims. The footnotes, however, are not applicable in this case, reinforcing the clarity of contents. The leading text contextualizes the table within a wider framework of operational instructions, indicating the structured overview of claims settlement for accounts with nomination, implying a categorization for clearer resolution processes as indicated in the surrounding content.</data>
