  <data key="d0">tb-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-0003</data>
  <data key="d1">table</data>
  <data key="d2">[Table Name]account_nomination_instructions

This table outlines the operational instructions regarding nominations for accounts held by individuals or jointly by multiple parties. There are 8 rows detailing various scenarios of account holders, with 5 columns categorizing the situation, the nominees, and the respective actions that can be taken upon the death of the account holders. The columns include 'Account in the Name of', 'Operational Instructions', 'Nominee', 'Situation', and 'What is to be done'. The table describes several cases, such as when person A dies, when person B dies, or when both account holders die. For instance, in the scenario where account A is held 'Either or Survivor' with nominee X, if A dies, the balance outstanding will be payable to B. Conversely, if both A and B die, X will receive the outstanding amount. The terms 'Self' and 'Jointly' in the operational instructions indicate provisions for individuals and joint accounts, respectively, with associated impacts on the nominees. Overall, the table captures essential guidance for managing account nominations and the implications arising from the death of account holders. It aligns with the context of customer service policies, emphasizing the importance of proper designation of nominees for account management. There are no null markers or outliers present in the data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-mm-table-002</data>
