  <data key="d1">table</data>
  <data key="d2">[Table Name]account_payable_instructions_after_death

This table outlines the operational instructions regarding account payments upon the death of account holders, detailing various scenarios based on single or joint accounts. There are four columns in the table: 'Account in the Name of,' 'Operational Instructions,' 'Situation,' and 'What is to be done.' The rows represent different cases involving either single account holders or joint account holders named A and B, each specifying the consequence upon the death of either party. For instance, if account A dies, as per the instruction 'Self,' the outstanding amount is payable to the legal heirs or any mandated individual among them. If both A and B are joint account holders and one of them dies, the outstanding is payable to the surviving joint account holder, and in the event both pass away, it is payable to their legal heirs. The table encapsulates essential protocols for handling account funds in different circumstances of account holder mortality, ensuring clarity in the claims process for beneficiaries. This information is part of a larger document related to customer service policies, as indicated by the leading and trailing context provided.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-mm-table-004</data>
