This table outlines the access protocols for lockers in the absence of a nomination, detailing the instructions for legal heirs or loved ones based on various scenarios regarding the owners A and B. The table consists of four columns: 'Locker in the Name of', 'Operational Instructions', 'Situation', and 'What is to be done'. It lists multiple rows specifying circumstances arising from the death of one or both individuals named A and B. The operational instructions categorize the scenarios into two types: 'Either or Survivor' and 'Jointly'. For example, if A dies, the legal heirs of A or any mandated individual may access the locker. In cases where both A and B die, their legal heirs are granted access. The document does not contain any numerical data or aggregate values, focusing instead on the procedures to be followed. This table serves as a guide for managing locker contents and the access rights of heirs in various death scenarios, illustrating how ownership and access change depending on who survives. The context of the table suggests it is part of a broader discussion on customer service policies relating to locker access and inheritance issues.</data>
