<node id="tb-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-0009">
  <data key="d0">tb-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-0009</data>
  <data key="d1">table</data>
  <data key="d2">[Table Name]settlement_claims_checklist

The table titled 'Checklist- Settlement of Claims in Safe Deposit Locker and Articles in Safe Custody by Deceased Customer' outlines the documentation required for processing claims related to safe deposit lockers and articles held in custody after the death of the customer, highlighting the distinctions between cases with and without nominees. The structure consists of several rows categorized under headings such as 'Claims with Nominee(s)/Survivorship(s)', 'Cases without Nominee/ Survivorship clause', and 'Settlement of Claims not falling under the Simplified Procedure', which are represented as broader claim categories. Each category specifies various required documents, including Claim Forms, Death Certificates, and Inventory Forms, along with designated annexure references, indicating which documents correspond to specific rules or guidelines for claims processing. For instance, the first category lists documents like the Claim Form and Death Certificate without an annexure, while the second highlights 'Claims falling under the simplified procedure' with a comprehensive breakdown into specific documents like the Disclaimer/No Objection Letter and multiple annexure references (I-B, I-D, I-E, and I-F). It also identifies claims related to probate of wills, underscoring the complexity of documentation required when legal inheritors contest claims. Patterns such as the repeated need for Claim Forms across various categories indicate the importance of this document in all claims. Notably, the table reveals several instances of missing or empty data, which might signify optional requirements or cases that do not apply, thus encouraging thorough verification of individual claim circumstances. Overall, this organized checklist serves as a critical tool for legal and administrative personnel managing claims post the demise of a customer, enhancing clarity in the documentation process while adhering to the internal policy guidelines outlined in the leading and trailing texts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2d2b1e01babacd5427ea9228ee35f7f9-mm-table-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Rules of Nomination &amp; Settlement of Claim 1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787741494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
